file_manager: folders that server.files.list doesn't walk

server.files.list walks a root recursively, on the event loop, and
get_path_info() costs ~14 ms per file on the AD5X (a resolve() and the
reserved path checks, Path.parents for each reserved path). Mainsail and
Fluidd ask for the config root at each page load. Since v0.1.0-rc1 the
config folder holds the "plugins" link to /data/ad5x/plugins
(kiln_os.link_plugins), so the list walks every installed plugin too:
with kiln-notify and afc-kiln (~2200 files) each page load blocked
Moonraker for about a minute (EVENT LOOP BLOCKED 56-58 s), the web UIs
stopped loading and the Klippy connection dropped.

add_unlisted_path() names a folder that get_file_list() doesn't enter
wherever it is reached in a root, through a link or not. The folders are
matched by device and inode, which the walk already reads for each
folder, so the check costs one stat per unlisted folder per list.
Clients still browse the folder with get_directory, its files can be
read, edited, uploaded and deleted as before, and inotify still watches
it; its files are only missing from the flat list. kiln_os registers the
plugins folder.

From PR #70 by DIEHARDave.

Upstream: not submitted (AD5X open OS)

